Have you tried http://myusername:mypassword@somesite.com in your browser ?

curl somesite.com --user username:password

curl -u myusername:mypassword http://somesite.com

You can use Postman a plugin for chrome. It gives the ability to choose the
 authentication type you need for each of the requests. In that menu you can
 configure user and password. Postman will automatically translate the config
 to a authentication header that will be sent with your request.

